ALLOWED_ORIGINS=http://localhost:3000,http://localhost:80


# ==============================================================================
# DEPLOYMENT INSTRUCTIONS
# ==============================================================================

QUICKSTART GUIDE:
=================

1. SETUP FILES:
   - Save your original agent code as: agent_code.py
   - Save the FastAPI backend as: api_server.py
   - Save the Dockerfile above as: Dockerfile
   - Save docker-compose.yml above
   - Save requirements.txt above
   - Save nginx.conf above (optional)
   - Save .env above

2. INSTALL DOCKER:
   - Windows/Mac: https://www.docker.com/products/docker-desktop
   - Linux: sudo apt install docker.io docker-compose

3. START SERVICES:
   docker-compose up -d

4. CHECK STATUS:
   docker-compose ps
   docker-compose logs -f agent

5. ACCESS:
   - API: http://localhost:8000
   - API Docs: http://localhost:8000/docs
   - Frontend: http://localhost:3000 (if using React)

6. STOP SERVICES:
   docker-compose down

7. VIEW LOGS:
   docker-compose logs -f

MANUAL DEPLOYMENT (without Docker):
====================================

1. Install dependencies:
   pip install -r requirements.txt

2. Start Ollama:
   ollama serve

3. Pull model:
   ollama pull llama3.1:8b

4. Start backend:
   python api_server.py

5. Access API:
   http://localhost:8000

PRODUCTION DEPLOYMENT:
======================

1. USE HTTPS:
   - Get SSL cert (Let's Encrypt)
   - Configure nginx with SSL
   - Update docker-compose ports

2. SECURITY:
   - Change all default passwords in .env
   - Set SECRET_KEY to random string
   - Configure firewall rules
   - Enable authentication

3. MONITORING:
   - Add Prometheus/Grafana
   - Configure log aggregation
   - Set up alerts

4. BACKUP:
   docker-compose exec agent tar -czf backup.tar.gz agent_memory agent_secure
   
5. SCALING:
   docker-compose up --scale agent=3

TROUBLESHOOTING:
================

Issue: Ollama not connecting
Fix: Check ollama logs: docker-compose logs ollama

Issue: Port already in use
Fix: Change ports in docker-compose.yml

Issue: Out of memory
Fix: Increase Docker memory limit in Docker Desktop settings

Issue: Model not found
Fix: docker-compose exec ollama ollama pull llama3.1:8b

CLOUD DEPLOYMENT:
=================

AWS:
- EC2 instance (t3.large minimum)
- ECS/EKS for container orchestration
- S3 for file storage
- RDS for PostgreSQL

Google Cloud:
- Compute Engine
- Cloud Run for containers
- Cloud Storage
- Cloud SQL

Azure:
- Virtual Machines
- Container Instances
- Blob Storage
- Azure Database

DigitalOcean:
- Droplet (4GB RAM minimum)
- Managed Kubernetes
- Spaces for storage
- Managed Database

COST ESTIMATES (Monthly):
=========================

Local (your computer): $0
- Uses local resources
- No cloud costs

VPS Deployment: $20-50
- DigitalOcean/Linode droplet
- 4GB RAM, 2 vCPU
- Local Ollama models

Cloud with APIs: $50-200
- Small VM for backend
- API calls to OpenAI/Claude
- Pay per use

Full Cloud Setup: $100-500
- Load balancer
- Auto-scaling
- Managed database
- Full monitoring